          "lyricsTranslation": "[Verse 1]\nYour face is reflected in the last train’s window.\nThe rain has stopped at the eaves; the city is still awake.\nYou fold an old train ticket into a little boat.\nYou say some goodbyes are another kind of shore.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOne by one, the streetlights fall away behind us.\nI softly sing the words I never said.\n\n[Chorus]\nMay the wind bring tomorrow to your side.\nMay starlight fall on every street you pass.\nEven if I cannot walk this road beside you,\nMay you look up and find a clear sky.\n\n[Verse 2]\nThe corner store’s lights stay on past midnight.\nThe scent of hot coffee drifts past old records.\nI tuck your smile into a bookmark.\nEvery page I open is still spring.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOne by one, the streetlights fall away behind us.\nI softly sing the words I never said.\n\n[Chorus]\nMay the wind bring tomorrow to your side.\nMay starlight fall on every street you pass.\nEven if I cannot walk this road beside you,\nMay you look up and find a clear sky.\n\n[Bridge]\nDo not fear the train that takes you somewhere unfamiliar.\nYou carry your own light; you will not be alone.\n\n[Final Chorus]\nMay the wind bring tomorrow to your side.\nMay starlight fall on every street you pass.\nEven if I cannot walk this road beside you,\nMay you look up and find a clear sky.\n\n[Outro]\nThe last train’s window slowly slips away.\nFacing tomorrow, I say goodbye.",
