          "lyrics": "[Verse 1]\nThe train rolls on, your face stays here with me\nI see a world that will not fall asleep\nYou make a boat from an old note you saved\nA soft goodbye gives each heart room to grow\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOne by one, the lights go dim and fade from view\nAll the words I could not say, I sing for you\n\n[Chorus]\nMay dawn find you safe and warm\nAs you go on, let stars be your light and guide\nIf I am far, know love is a road back home\nKeep me in mind when a new day calls your name\n\n[Verse 2]\nThe cafe lights stay on beside the square\nI hear the song we knew come through the rain\nI keep your smile among the lines I read\nEach page I turn brings back warm days of spring\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOne by one, the lights go dim and fade from view\nAll the words I could not say, I sing for you\n\n[Chorus]\nMay dawn find you safe and warm\nAs you go on, let stars be your light and guide\nIf I am far, know love is a road back home\nKeep me in mind when a new day calls your name\n\n[Bridge]\nThat same old star still shines the way back home\nSing that old tune; dreams rise and drift like snow\n\n[saxophone solo]\n\n[Final Chorus]\nMay dawn find you safe and warm\nAs you go on, let stars be your light and guide\nIf I am far, know love is a road back home\nKeep me in mind when a new day calls your name\n\n[Outro]\nThe train rolls on, your face stays here with me\nI say goodbye and greet a new day",
